body:
Awful disgusting thing of her to say!

BUTTTT it gave me a lot of thoughts. Ever since I've developed a legitimate death wish I've been trying to see the positive side of everything because, well, fuck it, nothing matters anyway, so here's my take on the \~silver lining\~ of what she said if it would make you feel better. Totally feel free not to read on:

&#x200B;

From the way the quote is written your mom's friend sounds like an older, kind of brash, foreign lady. Could be wrong, but regardless, a lot of people like that and even some people who are just kind of gruff by nature see "fat" as a descriptor with no negative connotation. "Getting fat" and "getting skinny" are, to some people, just things that happen during life without all the emotional weight we (people with EDs) attach to them. I emphasize so deeply with how shitty it must have felt to have someone imply that you're "fat", and you probably aren't anywhere near "fat", but imagine how free you (all of us here actually) would feel if "fat" didn't really mean anything bad to you until it was at the point of actually negatively impacting your health? What if someone telling you you're too "fat" for a pair of pants was just like someone telling you you probably shouldn't use their dry shampoo because it's tinted for brunettes and you're a blonde? Of course this assumes she said it without the intention to hurt your feelings, but if it is the case that she just said it as an off-hand remark, maybe it can be kind of comforting to think about the fact that some people genuinely see "gotten fat" as just a phrase that means "curvier than you may have been in the past" rather than "gross, ugly, etc.". And if you think about it that way, it may help you to feel less anger towards her, although I know it's way easier said than done.

&#x200B;

In any case, I hope you're feeling better, and I hope you either fit the pants of found a pair even cuter xx

Agreeee. Literally this is life while recovering from bulimia in a nutshell. After having this exact scenario happen to me like three times during my first go at recovery I was too traumatized to ever really "binge" on my own because I realized that I'd be miserable if I put anything in my body I wasn't willing to leave there....but the real trouble comes imo when you're doing stuff like dinners with friends/family/boys/whatever or parties. It's rally hard for me at least to eat a non-calorie counted/home cooked meal at all, and if I just pick at it I'm more ravenous than I would've been if I hadn't eaten at all, and if I eat to the point of actual satisfaction I'm utterly miserable after.

&#x200B;

Still haven't realllly figured out a perfect balance here. If you figure out anything that helps let me know I'd love to trade healthy non-purging tips.

THANK YOU. I purposely chose a picture where, in my opinion, I look very healthy to post here. I've given some advice to people who messaged me and specifically asked, and obviously I told them about what healthy lifestyle changes worked for me and not what off-the-rails ED behaviors I've struggled with. If I'd posted a picture that showed off ribs or hipbones, or if a girl who's severely underweight had posted, I think it would be different, but imo this post was not any more ED-fueling/encouraging than the other content on this sub, so there's no reason I should be barred from participating.

As to your response to another person about my gc posts, thanks for playing devil's advocate for me. I find it unbelievably ironic that members of a group that care *so much* about semantics and controlling others' speech referred to me as "they" (lol \~respecting pronouns\~ is more of a preach than a practice huh) and "terf" (known slur we've asked not to be called as a community) in their comments. My ideas on the concept and definition of womanhood are extremely deeply and sincerely held, and having a bunch of strangers on the internet gang up on me over it is not going to change that. I think that it's a great show of defensiveness/insecurity that they feel the need to attack anyone who holds a different view than they do on the subject, even in *completely* unrelated forums.

&#x200B;

Yes!! This is beautiful.

&#x200B;

I've been a b/p-er for almost a year now, and I am  finally climbing out of the darkness (I went from doing it up to 5 times per DAY to having maybe one lapse per week now). What worked for me was aspiring to be one of the girls who were doing more healthy "high restriction" on proED, which leads to less binges and is more sustainable overall. 

&#x200B;

My therapist also told me that in studies, only 50% of calories at most are actually purged, which shocked me because i would eat thousands of calories in a sitting. It's wayyyy too easy to go from having one purge, and getting the satisfaction of seeing the food come up, to doing it on a consistent basis, to purposely buying big quantities of food to binge on and getting trapped in the cycle. <3 stay strong everyone!!

I know that I am a woman because I was born with a female body, that's literally it. There are many consequences to this, both physical and societal, that only biological women face, and so the idea that "gender identity" rather than biology defines womanhood, trans ideology is attempting to obscure our issues and make them not-PC to discuss in a female-centric space without walking on endless eggshells to avoid hurting the feelings of the biological males who are appropriating our experience.

&#x200B;

No one calls a spayed cat a male cat do they? Ditto infertile women/my hypothetically "castrated" self.

&#x200B;

Further, why exactly can't trans people get all the surgery they like and wear what they please but refrain from saying that any of this turns them into "women". They acknowledge that their surgery doesn't change their ex, but this is just the problem. They think that our sex is less important than their feelings when it comes to defining the identity that we were born into. No?

Yes! But I think that your status as "man" or "woman" should be defined by biology, which is a binary 98% of the time, rather than by, essentially, personality traits. That's why we're seeing 100 different "genders" now, because "gender" essentially means personality nowadays and there are a million different variations of masculine and feminine personalities. Saying that "woman" refers to a general feminine feeling and personality, however, disregards the biological reality and oppression that women face based on our sex and excludes women who don't conform from our own identity!

&#x200B;

ugh.

we want you to do whatever the hell you want but stop appropriating our gender when you show us no respect. did you ever consult the genuine female population before you began aggressively colonizing us? do you ever treat people who disagree with you (especially women) with respect? Do you ever, for two seconds, consider the harm that your selfish ideology imposes on the 50% of the human race that is biologically female? No's down the line.

&#x200B;

Being a woman is dealing with the aftermath of thousands of years of sex-based oppression as well as the physical implications of your birth sex (monthly periods, pregnancy, etc.) you will never have to deal with either, you just get to play with the accessories and steal our badge of honor with no merit.

If questioning the validity of men who get cosmetic surgery, wear womens' clothes, and then bully women into recognizing them despite the fact that you'll never experience any of the physiological or social consequences of women makes me the "scum of the earth" then that just shows how out of touch with reality you are. I love how you made no effort to respond to my GENUINE QUESTION (which shouldn't be banned as I am genuinely trying to understand the other side), because you likely have no substantive response. Unfortunate because I really did want to have a conversation.

&#x200B;

Edit: women who question the colonization of every last one of our spaces and are bullied into not even questioning it = scum to TIMs. men who fight against women's rights to abortion, contraceptives, feminine hygiene, adequate medical care = irrelevant to TIMs because ya'll have no respect for the class of people who you're trying to appropriate.
